About Baringa&nbsp;

Baringa is a global consulting firm that partners with leaders to drive change and create value. With deep industry expertise, and enabled by advanced technology, the firm helps clients to deliver with greater confidence and certainty. With over 2,000 people across the UK, Europe, North America, Asia and Australia, the firm combines global insight with local understanding.

The firm works across energy and resources, financial services, government and public sector, consumer products and retail, pharmaceuticals and life sciences, manufacturing, and technology, media and telecoms, with capabilities spanning strategy, transformation and operational excellence - all powered by advanced technology, data, AI and digital innovation.

Clients value Baringa’s collaborative approach and the way its teams integrate seamlessly - all working with a shared understanding of what matters most. The firm is known for its kind, curious experts who listen closely and care deeply about client success as they help clients transform energy markets, modernise financial platforms, expand telecoms and digital networks through advanced data analytics, enable digital services in government, and unlock growth in consumer sectors.

Certified as a&nbsp; Great Place to Work around the world, Baringa has been recognised by the Financial Times in 22 categories of its UK Leading Management Consultants rankings, and by Forbes for four consecutive years as one of the World’s Best Management Consulting Firms.

Our Early Careers Team are looking for a Senior Early Careers Assistant for a 14 month FTC to join the team.

Key dates: From November 2026 - January 2028 (14 month FTC)

The Early Careers team &nbsp; is responsible for &nbsp;shaping the end-to-end Early Careers journey at Baringa, from attracting and recruiting talented individuals to onboarding and supporting their development. Working in partnership with the business, we deliver impactful and inclusive experiences that enable junior talent to thrive and build successful careers. &nbsp;

What you will be doing

You will support the end-to-end delivery of our Early Careers programmes, helping to attract, recruit, onboard, and develop talented Interns and Analysts across Baringa’s global offices. &nbsp;

Partnership Management &amp; Attraction &nbsp;

• Build and&nbsp;maintain&nbsp;strong relationships with Baringa's Early Careers attraction partners,&nbsp;ensuring maximum engagement and return on investment. &nbsp;

• Collaborate with&nbsp;our&nbsp;partners to promote Baringa's Early Careers opportunities and enhance our employer brand across diverse talent communities. &nbsp;

• Support the planning, coordination and delivery of university,&nbsp;school&nbsp;and college outreach initiatives. &nbsp;

Outreach &amp; Events &nbsp;

• Lead the planning and&nbsp;logistics&nbsp;for careers fairs, campus&nbsp;events&nbsp;and networking activities. &nbsp;

• Develop and&nbsp;maintain&nbsp;relationships with universities&nbsp;and schools&nbsp;to strengthen Baringa's Early Careers talent pipeline. &nbsp;

• Coordinate event materials, registrations, follow-up&nbsp;communications&nbsp;and stakeholder engagement to deliver high-quality candidate experiences. &nbsp;

Recruitment Delivery &nbsp;

• Support the end-to-end recruitment cycle for Intern and Analyst programmes&nbsp;across Baringa’s global offices. &nbsp;

• Screen applications, coordinate interviews, manage candidate&nbsp;communications&nbsp;and organise assessment centres. &nbsp;

• Partner with hiring managers and stakeholders to ensure an efficient,&nbsp;inclusive&nbsp;and positive recruitment process. &nbsp;

Onboarding &amp; Induction &nbsp;

• Support with&nbsp;the end-to-end onboarding process for all Interns and Analysts, ensuring a seamless transition into Baringa. &nbsp;

• Coordinate offer administration, pre-employment checks, onboarding&nbsp;communications&nbsp;and induction&nbsp;logistics. &nbsp;

